## 3. What we built

### The flow (5 steps, every step can be skipped and finished later)

| Step | Elena asks | What happens in the background |
|---|---|---|
| 0 · Start | Host opens the link (`/me` or `/en`) | Anonymous session is created, so memory works from the first second |
| 1 · Guests & description | "Describe your place and what kind of guests you like best" | Voice → text → Claude extracts preferred guests, vibe and selling points |
| 2 · Find the property | "What's your place called and where is it?" | Apify searches Google Maps, Booking and Airbnb → Elena shows a candidate card → after confirmation, full profile (photos, amenities, units, house rules, reviews) is pulled in |
| 3 · Other platforms & calendar | "Do you also list on other platforms?" | iCal link is validated and saved, so no double bookings |
| 4 · Price & payout | "What price per night do you want?" (suggestion from Booking) + explanation of the model: the host keeps their full price, the guest pays an 8% fee | Price, minimum stay and bank account are validated and saved |
| 5 · Licence & preview | "Take a photo of your registration licence" | OCR reads the licence and checks it against the data → host account via phone/email code → private preview of the profile |

At the end, the listing is exported in the Ugosti.me format (JSON/CSV) for the Ugosti.me team to import.

### UX principles
- One question per message, with quick-reply buttons
- The microphone is the main input. Elena always repeats what she understood ("Did I get that right?")
- Cards instead of forms. Nothing is blocking, everything can be done "later"
- Progress bar ("Step 3 of 6") and memory: if the host comes back, Elena continues where they left off
- Language is set by the link: Montenegrin/Serbian or English
- Optional "live conversation" mode with Elena's voice (ElevenLabs Agent)

### Architecture

```
elena.ugosti.me/me ─┐
elena.ugosti.me/en ─┴─▶ Lovable PWA (React) ◀── Realtime ── Supabase (Auth · Postgres · Storage · pgvector)
                           │                                        ▲
   chat / speech-to-text ──┤                                        │ drafts + memory
   live voice (WebRTC) ────┘                                        │
Supabase Edge Functions ─▶ n8n workflows ─▶ Claude (Haiku / Sonnet) ┤
                         ─▶ ElevenLabs (Scribe STT, TTS, Agents)    │
                   n8n ─▶ Apify actors (Google Maps, Booking, Airbnb)
                   n8n ─▶ export (JSON/CSV in Ugosti.me format) ─▶ Ugosti.me team
```

**Key design decision:** the flow is driven by a state machine in n8n/Supabase (`current_step`), not by a free-running AI agent. The LLM only does two things: extract structured data from the host's answer and, when needed, personalise the next message. This makes the flow predictable and much cheaper.

### Tools used
| Tool | Role |
|---|---|
| **Lovable** | Mobile web app (PWA), chat UI, cards, preview page |
| **Supabase** | Database, auth, file storage, memory, knowledge base (pgvector) |
| **n8n** | All business logic: step handler, property search, scraping, mapping, export |
| **ElevenLabs** | Speech-to-text (Scribe), Elena's voice (TTS), live voice agents ME/EN |
| **Apify** | Finding the property and pulling its data from Google Maps, Booking, Airbnb |
| **Claude API** | Data extraction (Haiku), listing description (Sonnet), licence OCR |
| **GitHub** | This repository |

